Memory type: semantic_memory
Recorded: 2026-08-14
Confidence: 0.98
Owner: Marcus Reed
Tags: vllm, batch-api, compatibility, validation, silent-failure

## Summary

When a batch endpoint documents non-streaming operation and does not propagate tool definitions, requests with stream=true or non-null tools must fail request-model validation with a clear 4xx-compatible parameter error. Do not allow them into rendering or collection, where they can produce misleading HTTP 200 responses with empty or silently incomplete results. Preserve omitted/false stream and omitted/null tools for supported batch requests.

## Outcome

vLLM #50026 fixed in the pinned internal snapshot with focused request-model coverage.

